{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport inspect\nimport tensorcircuit as tc\nfrom tensorcircuit import gates\nprint(inspect.getsource(gates.exponential_gate_unity))\nprint('---')\nprint(inspect.getsource(gates.exponential_gate))\nPY\nrg -n \\\"def exp|non_unitary|is_unitary|unitary=False|normalize\\\" /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/circuit.py | head -40\nrg -n \\\"def state|def wavefunction|def expectation|renormal|norm\\\" /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/tensorcircuit/basecircuit.py | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"@partial(arg_alias, alias_dict={\"unitary\": [\"hermitian\", \"hamiltonian\"]})\ndef exponential_gate_unity(\n    unitary: Tensor, theta: float, half: bool = False, name: str = \"none\"\n) -> Gate:\n    r\"\"\"\n    Faster exponential gate directly implemented based on RHS. Only works when :math:`U^2 = I` is an identity matrix.\n\n    .. math::\n        \\textrm{exp}(U) &= e^{-j \\theta U} \\\\\n                &= \\cos(\\theta) I - j \\sin(\\theta) U \\\\\n\n    :param unitary: input unitary :math:`U`\n    :type unitary: Tensor\n    :param theta: angle in radians\n    :type theta: float\n    :param half: if True, the angel theta is mutiplied by 1/2,\n        defaults to False\n    :type half: bool\n    :param name: suffix of Gate name\n    :type name: str, optional\n    :return: Exponential Gate\n    :rtype: Gate\n    \"\"\"\n    theta, unitary = num_to_tensor(theta, unitary)\n    size = int(reduce(mul, unitary.shape))\n    n = int(np.log2(size))\n    i = np.eye(2 ** (int(n / 2)))\n    i_reshaped = i.reshape([2] * n)\n    unitary = backend.reshape(unitary, [2] * n)\n    it = array_to_tensor(i_reshaped)\n    if half is True:\n        theta = theta / 2.0\n    mat = backend.cos(theta) * it - 1.0j * backend.sin(theta) * unitary\n    return Gate(mat, name=\"exp1-\" + name)\n\n---\n@partial(arg_alias, alias_dict={\"unitary\": [\"hermitian\", \"hamiltonian\"]})\ndef exponential_gate(unitary: Tensor, theta: float, name: str = \"none\") -> Gate:\n    r\"\"\"\n    Exponential gate.\n\n    .. math::\n        \\textrm{exp}(U) = e^{-j \\theta U}\n\n    :param unitary: input unitary :math:`U`\n    :type unitary: Tensor\n    :param theta: angle in radians\n    :type theta: float\n    :param name: suffix of Gate name\n    :return: Exponential Gate\n    :rtype: Gate\n    \"\"\"\n    theta, unitary = num_to_tensor(theta, unitary)\n    mat = backend.expm(-backend.i() * theta * unitary)\n    dimension = reduce(mul, mat.shape)\n    nolegs = int(np.log(dimension) / np.log(2))\n    mat = backend.reshape(mat, shape=[2] * nolegs)\n    return Gate(mat, name=\"exp-\" + name)\n\n198:        Middle measurement in z-basis on the circuit, note the wavefunction output is not normalized\n199:        with ``mid_measurement`` involved, one should normalize the state manually if needed.\n680:        krausf: Callable[..., Sequence[Gate]], is_unitary: bool = False\n695:            if not is_unitary:\n704:                self._qir[-1][\"channel_unitary\"] = is_unitary\n712:                is_unitary = True\n714:                is_unitary = False\n719:                    getattr(channels, k + \"channel\"), is_unitary=is_unitary\n874:    def expectation(\n961:def expectation(\n383:    def expectation_before(\n1865:        return backend.reshape(t.tensor / backend.norm(t.tensor), [-1])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
